A||||6||Robert||Computer help needed... word file will not open||||5||
Z||000000||Robert||09-16-2001||01:42 PM||||My sister sent me a file that she somehow messed up.  She says she was just typing and when she looked up the page was blank.  She had been saving the file at every page break, and the file she sent me is 19kb, but nothing comes up on my screen.<BR>Any ideas? <BR>I have uploaded the file to the link below.<P>Thanks in advance.<BR>Robert<P><BR> <A HREF="http://www.canterburytrails.com/word/western" TARGET=_blank>www.canterburytrails.com/word/western</A>  civilization 2001.doc||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||09-16-2001||02:22 PM||||<B><FONT COLOR="red">Caution!</FONT></B> Opening Word files <B>can</B> install a virus on your computer. I'm not saying this file has a virus, but take extra caution when opening files downloaded from the internet.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Robert||09-16-2001||02:51 PM||||Sorry Cliff, I never even thought of a virus.  <BR>In the past she has sent me files, and Norton has never picked up the hint of a virus.||||reg||1
Z||000003||thomas_l||09-16-2001||05:03 PM||||Open it in Notepad. If you're lucky, there will be enough useable text to copy & paste into a new doc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-16-2001||06:29 PM||||Ummm... 19K is about the normal overhead in a word file. You might be able to salvage it in notepad but in all reality it's probably gone.<P>I usually tell people to use save as every so often to keep a couple different copies of critical files. Word and Excell are both great for hosing documents.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Robert||09-17-2001||02:40 PM||||Thanks for the advice everyone.  Fortunately my sister has a recent printout, so she is busy retyping and editing for her Thursday class.<BR>Robert<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Taijiguy||09-18-2001||09:17 AM||||Word automatically saves rescue documents every so often, generally every 10 minutes I think is default. She can do a search for rescue docs. The names used and storage location are differnt depending on the version of Windows and Word. She can find the location by looking under Tools-&gt;Options-&gt;File Locations. She might find a recovery document there.||||reg||1
